SUMMARY="Sandboxed and extendable image loading"
DESCRIPTION="Glycin allows to decode, edit, and create images and read metadata. On Linux, decoding \
happens in sandboxed modular image loaders. We use the term 'image loader' for simplicity, but image \
loaders also handle image editing and creation.
* glycin – The Rust image library
* libglycin – C-Bindings for the library
* libglycin-gtk4 – C-Bindings to convert glycin frames to GDK Textures
* libglycin-rebind - Safe Rust bindings to libglycin


glycin-loaders – Glycin loaders for several formats
glycin-thumbnailer – Glycin thumbnailer using the installed loaders

Bindings for other languages:
* GJS
* Python"
HOMEPAGE="https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glycin"
COPYRIGHT="2026 Sophie Herold"
LICENSE="MPL v2.0"
REVISION="1"
